[style name="our style"]
join renko leftmost
renko: Ugh, what the…ow…
join merry rightmost
merry: Renko, you’re okay! Thank goodness, you had me really worried.
yukari: Yeah, yeah I’m good, I think. Head hurts and legs too…other than that I think nothing’s broken.
renko: But what the heck happened, where are we? And how did we get here?
merry: I’m…not sure
merry: We were just walking home and then everything went dark.
merry: When I came to we were in this strange place and you were passed out on the floor.
merry: I didn’t want to leave you to look for help so I’ve just been waiting next to you.
renko: Damn, I don’t remember any of that at all…But what about you? Are you at least okay?
merry: I…think so?
renko: Whew, well that’s good.
renko: But man, this place is familiar…Have we been here before? I can just barely make them out, but are those plants?
merry: They seem to be.
merry: Even with this stale air and lack of wind this place still feels close to nature in a way. It reminds me of the TORIFUNE.
renko: Oh, the microhabitat satellite? Do you think your barrier powers activated randomly and sent us here?
merry: It’s possible.
merry: But I do think we need to find a way out of here and quickly. I keep hearing these really strange sounds.
renko: Strange how?
merry: I’m not sure how to explain. It sort of sounds like a bird, but at the same time not really. It’s too…hollow, too sad.
merry: Either way, it’s not normal sounding. Whatever has been making it has been moving too. Sometimes it sounds very close, other times far away.
renko: Ah, a wild animal then? Or maybe something worse.
merry: Do you think it’s a youkai?
renko: Highly possible, considering what happened last time.
merry: Then it would be best to get going sooner rather than later. I am worried though. It might be a tad too dark to move around safely.
renko: Hmm yeah...Wait a sec! I’ve got this!
merry: Oh, a flashlight? Wonderful!
renko: It’s kinda cheap so it’s not the best one in the world, but we’ll at least be able to tell where we’re putting our feet.
renko: Still watch your step. I don't need you falling into any holes or gaps on me.
merry: Well I don’t plan on it, but I’ll stick as close as possible to you.
renko: Great, let’s get going. No idea how long this thing will last.